343 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 268 0 R
/T (CampusConnect is a full-stack campus event aggregation and student registration platform designed to centralize discovery, controlled event administration, organizer workflows, and engagement telemetry for a university environment. The system replaces fragmented event discovery across clubs, departments, social channels, and external forms with a single web application backed by a relational database. The core runtime uses Spring Boot, Spring Security, Spring Data JPA, Hibernate, MySQL, and Flyway, while the modern frontend is implemented with React, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, React Query, and form-validation tooling. Legacy Thymeleaf templates are retained for selected server-rendered flows.)
/E (CampusConnect is a full-stack campus event aggregation and student registration platform designed to centralize discovery, controlled event administration, organizer workflows, and engagement telemetry for a university environment. The system replaces fragmented event discovery across clubs, departments, social channels, and external forms with a single web application backed by a relational database. The core runtime uses Spring Boot, Spring Security, Spring Data JPA, Hibernate, MySQL, and Flyway, while the modern frontend is implemented with React, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, React Query, and form-validation tooling. Legacy Thymeleaf templates are retained for selected server-rendered flows.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
344 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 268 0 R
/T (The platform supports event search and category filtering, event detail views, role-based administration, club- scoped organizer workspaces, event creation and lifecycle management, external registration redirection, attendance check-in, CSV export, explainable event recommendations, and real-time Server-Sent Events \(SSE\) for capacity and organizer check-in telemetry. Database integrity is enforced through primary keys, foreign keys, unique constraints, CHECK constraints, indexes, and Flyway migrations. Registration workflows use a database uniqueness invariant on \(user_id, event_id\), while service-level pessimistic locking is used for concurrency-sensitive operations.)
/E (The platform supports event search and category filtering, event detail views, role-based administration, club- scoped organizer workspaces, event creation and lifecycle management, external registration redirection, attendance check-in, CSV export, explainable event recommendations, and real-time Server-Sent Events \(SSE\) for capacity and organizer check-in telemetry. Database integrity is enforced through primary keys, foreign keys, unique constraints, CHECK constraints, indexes, and Flyway migrations. Registration workflows use a database uniqueness invariant on \(user_id, event_id\), while service-level pessimistic locking is used for concurrency-sensitive operations.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 268 0 R
/T (The repository also contains evidence for database engineering concepts such as normalization, query optimization, concurrency stress testing, transactional outbox design, and operational observability. The latest main-branch GitHub Actions run reviewed for this report completed successfully across frontend verification, backend verification, and security scanning. At the same time, the repository contains some transition-state inconsistencies - notably between the documented runtime versions and the current Maven/CI configuration, and between the standalone schema.sql description and the later V5 multi-role/club migration. These have been recorded as limitations rather than silently reconciled. Overall, CampusConnect demonstrates a layered modular-monolith architecture with a strong academic emphasis on relational integrity, secure access control, testability, and deployment reproducibility.)
/E (The repository also contains evidence for database engineering concepts such as normalization, query optimization, concurrency stress testing, transactional outbox design, and operational observability. The latest main-branch GitHub Actions run reviewed for this report completed successfully across frontend verification, backend verification, and security scanning. At the same time, the repository contains some transition-state inconsistencies - notably between the documented runtime versions and the current Maven/CI configuration, and between the standalone schema.sql description and the later V5 multi-role/club migration. These have been recorded as limitations rather than silently reconciled. Overall, CampusConnect demonstrates a layered modular-monolith architecture with a strong academic emphasis on relational integrity, secure access control, testability, and deployment reproducibility.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
