461 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 271 0 R
/T (University event information is commonly distributed across student clubs, departmental notices, social platforms, messaging groups, and external registration forms. This fragmentation makes it difficult for students to discover events consistently and makes it harder for administrators to maintain a reliable view of event lifecycle, registrations, capacity, and participation. CampusConnect was designed as a centralized campus event catalogue and management platform that brings these workflows into a single database-backed system.)
/E (University event information is commonly distributed across student clubs, departmental notices, social platforms, messaging groups, and external registration forms. This fragmentation makes it difficult for students to discover events consistently and makes it harder for administrators to maintain a reliable view of event lifecycle, registrations, capacity, and participation. CampusConnect was designed as a centralized campus event catalogue and management platform that brings these workflows into a single database-backed system.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 271 0 R
/T (The repository description positions CampusConnect as a full-stack event management middleware for universities. Its implemented scope extends beyond a basic CRUD catalogue: the current codebase includes role-based access control, organizer club workspaces, event recommendations, attendance check-in, real-time SSE telemetry, transactional event publishing records, observability endpoints, and automated verification through GitHub Actions.)
/E (The repository description positions CampusConnect as a full-stack event management middleware for universities. Its implemented scope extends beyond a basic CRUD catalogue: the current codebase includes role-based access control, organizer club workspaces, event recommendations, attendance check-in, real-time SSE telemetry, transactional event publishing records, observability endpoints, and automated verification through GitHub Actions.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
463 0 obj
<<
