/P 271 0 R
/T (1.2 Problem Statement)
/E (1.2 Problem Statement)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 271 0 R
/T (The primary problem is the absence of a single, controlled source of truth for campus events and their associated user interest records. Students need to search and filter events, inspect event details, and follow an authoritative registration path. Administrators need privileged event management, analytics, and export capabilities. Club organizers need scoped access to their own events and attendee information. The system must perform these operations without allowing unauthorized mutation or duplicate user-event registration records.)
/E (The primary problem is the absence of a single, controlled source of truth for campus events and their associated user interest records. Students need to search and filter events, inspect event details, and follow an authoritative registration path. Administrators need privileged event management, analytics, and export capabilities. Club organizers need scoped access to their own events and attendee information. The system must perform these operations without allowing unauthorized mutation or duplicate user-event registration records.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
