588 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 275 0 R
/T (The core relational store is MySQL using the InnoDB storage engine. The documented master SQL schema contains `users`, `events`, `registrations`, and `outbox_events`. Flyway migrations V1 through V5 extend this structure, with V5 adding a `clubs` table and multi-role/club/check-in fields. The schema uses primary keys, foreign keys, unique constraints, CHECK constraints, and secondary B-tree indexes. Registration uniqueness is enforced by the composite key `\(user_id, event_id\)`.)
/E (The core relational store is MySQL using the InnoDB storage engine. The documented master SQL schema contains `users`, `events`, `registrations`, and `outbox_events`. Flyway migrations V1 through V5 extend this structure, with V5 adding a `clubs` table and multi-role/club/check-in fields. The schema uses primary keys, foreign keys, unique constraints, CHECK constraints, and secondary B-tree indexes. Registration uniqueness is enforced by the composite key `\(user_id, event_id\)`.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
