961 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 286 0 R
/T (`database/schema.sql` describes a four-table core schema, while Flyway V5 adds the `clubs` table, multi-role user fields, event club ownership, and registration check-in/ticket fields. Several design documents still describe the older four-table model. This is a valid architectural evolution, but the documentation package has not been fully synchronized with the latest migration. The present report explicitly records this difference instead of treating the older ER/data dictionary as the complete current runtime model.)
/E (`database/schema.sql` describes a four-table core schema, while Flyway V5 adds the `clubs` table, multi-role user fields, event club ownership, and registration check-in/ticket fields. Several design documents still describe the older four-table model. This is a valid architectural evolution, but the documentation package has not been fully synchronized with the latest migration. The present report explicitly records this difference instead of treating the older ER/data dictionary as the complete current runtime model.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
