/Title (The repository contains `firebase.json` and `.firebaserc` configuration for Firebase Hosting. The hosting target is configured to serve `frontend-redesign/dist` with a catch-all rewrite to `index.html`, making it suitable for SPA routing. Firestore rules and indexes are also present, but the primary CampusConnect relational runtime remains the Spring/MySQL system. The Firebase configuration should therefore be treated as an auxiliary hosting/integration layer rather than as a replacement for the core database.)
/Dest [31 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2058 0 R
>>
endobj
2081 0 obj
<<
/Title (`database/schema.sql` describes a four-table core schema, while Flyway V5 adds the `clubs` table, multi-role user fields, event club ownership, and registration check-in/ticket fields. Several design documents still describe the older four-table model. This is a valid architectural evolution, but the documentation package has not been fully synchronized with the latest migration. The present report explicitly records this difference instead of treating the older ER/data dictionary as the complete current runtime model.)
